summary: Run the upstream test suite
description: |
    Verify that jose passes its upstream test suite. By default, fetch the
    source RPM, apply distribution patches, build it, and run its tests. A
    configured JOSE_BUILD_DIR can be used to run the suite against an existing
    upstream build. When JOSE_REQUIRE_PQC_TESTS is enabled, require the ML-KEM
    Meson tests to be present and pass.
contact: Patrik Koncity <pkoncity@redhat.com>
test: ./runtest.sh
require:
  - jose
  - dnf-utils
  - gawk
  - grep
  - patch
  - bzip2
  - meson
  - ninja-build
  - openssl-devel
  - pkgconf-pkg-config
  - python3
duration: 10m
enabled: true
order: 20
tag:
  - CI-Tier-1
  - NoRHEL4
  - NoRHEL5
  - NoRHEL6
  - NoRHEL7
  - TIPfail
  - TIPfail_Security
  - fedora-wanted
extra-summary: /jose-tests/Sanity/upstream-test-suite
extra-task: /jose-tests/Sanity/upstream-test-suite
adjust:
  - enabled: false
    when: distro < rhel-8
    continue: false
id: 93d0c9f5-c5ea-45e9-9234-4bfd66052c7f
